        "prefix_token_count": 342,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: We can find the modular inverse of 2 modulo 83 using the Extended Euclidean Algorithm or by simple inspection. Since \\(2 \\cdot 41 = 82 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{83}\\), we have \\(2 \\cdot (-41) \\equiv 1 \\pmod{83}\\). Thus, the modular inverse of 2 modulo 83 is \\(-41\\), which is equivalent to \\(42\\) modulo 83 (since \\(-41 + 83 = 42\\))."
      },
